# Onec Development Standards

This is optional guidance for the main onec-context skill. Load
[the reference](reference.md) when this topic is relevant. Executable tools live
in the main skill or an exported bundle, not in this supplemental directory.
Resolve their actual location before running a command. Do not assume that
`onec-context` is installed on PATH.

Use the project's explicit conventions first. For a claim about an ITS rule,
query the separately prepared `standards` pack and cite the article or stored
source. Platform HBK does not automatically supply development standards.

For the installed toolkit, prepare a known local ITS directory with `ensure
--workspace-root /path/to/project --need standards --standards-dir
/path/to/its-v8std`, then use `query-kb --workspace-root /path/to/project --role
standards --q "topic" --json`. Resolve script paths from the main skill root.
In an exported bundle, resolve role `standards` and query the returned path with
`tools/local_kb_query.py --db`; the bundle cannot build a missing pack.

Retrieve only the articles relevant to the change. Distinguish mandatory project
rules, cited ITS guidance and your own recommendations. Do not invent rule
numbers or treat an empty search as proof that no rule applies.

Check API facts against the platform pack, project structures against metadata,
and behavior against code. Run the project's BSL diagnostics and relevant tests
after edits. Standards lookup alone does not validate a module.

The toolkit's ITS downloader requires access to the selected source and can
fail on authentication or unavailable pages. Do not promise that installation
downloads all ITS content. Local articles and configuration code remain within
the user's agreed data boundary.
